@* CreateProduct.razor — Phase 3.3 (Admin product creation)

   Staff-facing product creation page at route `/Admin/Products/Create`.
   Reached from the "Create product" button on /Admin/Products. Role-gated
   to Admin / Manager / Employee via [Authorize(Roles=...)].

   PURPOSE:
     Lets staff add a new product to the catalog so they can test the full
     shopping flow (browse → detail → add to cart → cart → submit). Without
     this page, there's no way to seed test data via the UI — only direct DB
     inserts or migrations could create products.

   FORM FIELDS:
     1. Name              (required, 1-200 chars)
     2. Description       (required, 1-2000 chars, multiline)
     3. Price Amount      (required, > 0)
     4. Price Currency    (required, 3-letter ISO 4217 — dropdown with the
                           most common currencies; user can also type a
                           custom 3-letter code)
     5. Initial Stock     (required, >= 0, <= 1,000,000)
     6. Category          (required — top-level category dropdown)
     7. SubCategory       (optional — filtered by selected Category)
     8. SubSubCategory    (optional — filtered by selected SubCategory)
     9. Picture           (optional — single image upload, JPEG/PNG/WebP,
                           max 5 MB. Held in memory until submit; only
                           saved to /uploads/products/ when "Create
                           product" is clicked.)

   VALIDATION:
     - FluentValidation runs server-side via Wolverine's pipeline (the
       CreateProductCommandValidator is registered with Wolverine's
       UseFluentValidation integration). The validator produces the
       first wave of error messages.
     - The handler does additional business-rule validation: name
       uniqueness, category hierarchy consistency. These produce
       user-friendly Result.Failure messages.
     - Client-side validation is minimal — we rely on RadzenFormField's
       Required + Min/Max for the basic checks (HTML5 form validation
       via EditForm's ValidationMessage). The authoritative check is
       always server-side.

   FORM SUBMISSION:
     - On valid submit: dispatch CreateProductCommand via Wolverine.
     - On success: toast + navigate to /Admin/Products (where the new
       product now appears in the list).
     - On failure: show the result.Error message inline at the top of
       the form. Field-level errors from FluentValidation are surfaced
       via EditContext validation.

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings via IStringLocalizer<CreateProduct> (Loc).
     Keys defined in CreateProduct.en-US.resx + CreateProduct.fa-IR.resx.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Required — this page uses EditForm with a POST-equivalent submit
     handler. The [AntiforgeryValidation] attribute on the page (via
     EditForm's built-in support) ensures the circuit's anti-forgery
     token is checked. Blazor Server circuits already have this token
     established at circuit-start; EditForm validates it automatically. *@

@page "/Admin/Products/Create"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")]
@using System.Globalization
@using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Interfaces
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.CreateProduct
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Queries.GetActiveCategories
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@using TakOne.WebUI.Extensions
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject ICurrentUserService CurrentUser
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<CreateProduct> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject HttpClient Http

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .create-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 2rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .create-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1.25rem;
                }
            }

            .form-section {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                gap: 1.25rem;
            }

            .price-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                align-items: flex-end;
            }

                .price-row .price-amount {
                    flex: 1 1 auto;
                }

                .price-row .price-currency {
                    flex: 0 0 120px;
                }

            .category-row {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                align-items: flex-end;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

                .category-row > * {
                    flex: 1 1 200px;
                    min-width: 180px;
                }

            .form-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.75rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                margin-top: 1rem;
            }

            .form-error {
                margin-bottom: 1rem;
            }

            /* ── Image upload area ──
                           Modern dropzone-style container. Big, inviting, with icon +
                           headline + helper text. The native <input type="file">
                           rendered by Blazor's InputFile component sits inside this
                           container; we style its ::file-selector-button pseudo-element
                           so it looks like a primary CTA that matches the rest of the
                           Radzen-styled page. */
            .upload-area {
                padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
                border: 2px dashed var(--rz-border-base-color);
                border-radius: 12px;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                text-align: center;
                transition: border-color 0.2s, background-color 0.2s, transform 0.1s;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.5rem;
            }

                .upload-area:hover {
                    border-color: var(--rz-primary);
                    background: var(--rz-primary-light);
                }

                .upload-area .upload-icon {
                    font-size: 2.5rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
                }

                .upload-area .upload-headline {
                    font-weight: 600;
                    color: var(--rz-text-color);
                }

                .upload-area .upload-hint {
                    font-size: 0.85rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                }

                /* Style the InputFile's native file input button to match
                           the Radzen primary button look. ::file-selector-button is
                           the standard pseudo-element supported by all modern
                           browsers (Chrome 119+, Firefox, Safari, Edge) for styling
                           the file-picker button on a file input. We keep the native
                           input (rather than hiding it and using a wrapping label
                           element) so keyboard focus and screen-reader behavior
                           work out of the box. */
                .upload-area .upload-input {
                    margin-top: 0.75rem;
                    max-width: 100%;
                }

                    .upload-area .upload-input::file-selector-button {
                        padding: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
                        margin-inline-end: 0.5rem;
                        border: 1px solid var(--rz-primary);
                        border-radius: var(--rz-border-radius);
                        background: var(--rz-primary);
                        color: var(--rz-primary-contrast-text-color, #fff);
                        font-weight: 500;
                        font-size: 0.95rem;
                        cursor: pointer;
                        transition: background-color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
                    }

                        .upload-area .upload-input::file-selector-button:hover {
                            background: var(--rz-primary-dark, var(--rz-primary));
                            border-color: var(--rz-primary-dark, var(--rz-primary));
                        }

                        .upload-area .upload-input::file-selector-button:disabled {
                            opacity: 0.6;
                            cursor: not-allowed;
                        }

            /* Preview card — REPLACES the dropzone once the user has
                           picked a file. Shows a downscaled thumbnail (generated
                           client-side via IBrowserFile.RequestImageFileAsync), the
                           filename + size, and a Remove button. The actual upload
                           to the server happens later, when the user submits the
                           form — so the card shows "selected" not "uploaded". */
            .preview-card {
                display: flex;
                gap: 1rem;
                align-items: stretch;
                padding: 1rem;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-border-base-color);
                border-radius: 8px;
            }

                .preview-card .preview-img-wrap {
                    flex: 0 0 140px;
                    width: 140px;
                    height: 140px;
                    display: flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    justify-content: center;
                    background: var(--rz-secondary-background-color);
                    border-radius: 6px;
                    overflow: hidden;
                }

                .preview-card .preview-img {
                    max-width: 100%;
                    max-height: 100%;
                    object-fit: contain;
                }

                .preview-card .preview-info {
                    flex: 1 1 auto;
                    display: flex;
                    flex-direction: column;
                    gap: 0.5rem;
                    min-width: 0;
                    justify-content: center;
                }

                    .preview-card .preview-info .preview-label {
                        font-weight: 600;
                        color: var(--rz-text-color);
                        display: flex;
                        align-items: center;
                        gap: 0.35rem;
                    }

                    .preview-card .preview-info .preview-url {
                        font-family: monospace;
                        font-size: 0.8rem;
                        color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                        word-break: break-all;
                        background: var(--rz-secondary-background-color);
                        padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
                        border-radius: 4px;
                    }

                .preview-card .preview-actions {
                    flex: 0 0 auto;
                    display: flex;
                    align-items: center;
                }

            /* Help panel on the right */
            .help-panel {
                position: sticky;
                top: 1rem;
            }

                .help-panel ul {
                    margin: 0.5rem 0 0 0;
                    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                    line-height: 1.7;
                }

                .help-panel li {
                    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
                }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .help-panel {
                    position: static;
                }
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Breadcrumb + back button ── *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem">
        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToManageProducts"]"
                      Icon="arrow_back"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                      Variant="Variant.Text"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
        <RadzenIcon Icon="add_box" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Loading state (categories still loading) ── *@
    @if (_isLoadingCategories)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["LoadingCategories"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Category-load failure state ──
       If categories fail to load, we can't show the form (Category is a
       required field that depends on this data). Show an error with a
       retry button instead of letting the user fill out the form and
       get a server-side "Category not found" error on submit. *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_categoriesLoadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_categoriesLoadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadCategoriesAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── No categories exist yet ──
       Categories must exist before products can be created (CategoryId is
       required). If the catalog has no categories yet, we redirect the user
       to create one first. (Phase X will add /Admin/Categories for this.) *@
    else if (_categories.Count == 0)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["NoCategoriesTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["NoCategoriesMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadCategoriesAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Main form ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="create-grid">
            @* LEFT — form fields *@
            <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.5rem;">
                <EditForm Model="@_model" OnValidSubmit="@HandleSubmitAsync" FormName="createProduct">
                    <DataAnnotationsValidator />

                    @* Server-side error banner (e.g. "Product name already exists") *@
                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_submitError))
                    {
                        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                                     Text="@_submitError"
                                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                     ShowIcon="true"
                                     Class="form-error" />
                    }

                    <div class="form-section">
                        @* Name *@
                        <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldName"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                            <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_model.Name"
                                           Placeholder="@Loc["FieldNamePlaceholder"]"
                                           TValue="string"
                                           Style="width: 100%;" />
                        </RadzenFormField>
                        <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.Name)" />

                        @* Description *@
                        <div>
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldDescription"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenTextArea @bind-Value="_model.Description"
                                                Placeholder="@Loc["FieldDescriptionPlaceholder"]"
                                                TValue="string"
                                                Rows="4"
                                                Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.Description)" />
                        </div>

                        @* Price (amount + currency) *@
                        <div>
                            <div class="price-row">
                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldPriceAmount"]" Class="price-amount">
                                    <RadzenNumeric TValue="decimal"
                                                   @bind-Value="_model.PriceAmount"
                                                   Min="0.01m"
                                                   Step="1"
                                                   Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>
                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldPriceCurrency"]" Class="price-currency">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="string"
                                                    @bind-Value="_model.PriceCurrency"
                                                    Data="_currencyOptions"
                                                    AllowFiltering="true"
                                                    AllowCustomValue="true"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["CurrencyPlaceholder"]"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>
                            </div>
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.PriceAmount)" />
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.PriceCurrency)" />
                        </div>

                        @* Initial stock *@
                        <div>
                            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldInitialStock"]" Style="width: 100%;">
                                <RadzenNumeric TValue="int"
                                               @bind-Value="_model.InitialStockQuantity"
                                               Min="0"
                                               Step="1"
                                               Style="width: 100%;" />
                            </RadzenFormField>
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.InitialStockQuantity)" />
                        </div>

                        @* Category hierarchy — three dropdowns in a row.
                           SubCategory is filtered to those whose CategoryId matches
                           the selected Category. SubSubCategory is filtered to those
                           whose SubCategoryId matches the selected SubCategory.
                           Selecting a new Category clears SubCategory + SubSubCategory
                           (the cascade invalidates the lower levels). Selecting a new
                           SubCategory clears SubSubCategory. *@
                        <div>
                            <div class="category-row">
                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldCategory"]">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    Value="_model.CategoryId"
                                                    Data="_categories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["CategoryPlaceholder"]"
                                                    ValueChanged="@OnCategoryChanged"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>

                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldSubCategory"]">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    Value="_model.SubCategoryId"
                                                    Data="_availableSubCategories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    AllowClear="true"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["OptionalPlaceholder"]"
                                                    ValueChanged="@OnSubCategoryChanged"
                                                    Disabled="@(_model.CategoryId == null)"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>

                                <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["FieldSubSubCategory"]">
                                    <RadzenDropDown TValue="Guid?"
                                                    @bind-Value="_model.SubSubCategoryId"
                                                    Data="_availableSubSubCategories"
                                                    TextProperty="Name"
                                                    ValueProperty="Id"
                                                    AllowClear="true"
                                                    Placeholder="@Loc["OptionalPlaceholder"]"
                                                    Disabled="@(_model.SubCategoryId == null)"
                                                    Style="width: 100%;" />
                                </RadzenFormField>
                            </div>
                            <ValidationMessage For="@(() => _model.CategoryId)" />
                        </div>

                        @* Picture (optional) — DEFERRED upload.
                           Visual design: a modern dropzone with icon +
                           headline + hint. When the user picks a file, we
                           capture it in memory as an IBrowserFile and
                           generate a small data-URL preview thumbnail — but
                           we do NOT upload it yet. The file is only sent to
                           the server when the user clicks "Create product"
                           (see HandleSubmitAsync). If the user cancels,
                           picks a different file, or fails client-side
                           validation, NO file is ever written to disk.
                           This fixes the original bug where every selected
                           image was immediately saved to /uploads/products/,
                           leaving orphan files when the form was never
                           submitted. *@
                        <div>
                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle2"
                                        Style="font-weight: 600; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                @Loc["FieldPictureUrl"]
                            </RadzenText>

                            @* Dropzone-style upload area — hidden once a
                               file is selected. The user can click "Remove"
                               on the preview to bring the dropzone back. *@
                            @if (_selectedFile is null)
                            {
                                <div class="upload-area">
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="cloud_upload" Class="upload-icon" />
                                    <div class="upload-headline">@Loc["UploadHeadline"]</div>
                                    <div class="upload-hint">@Loc["UploadHint"]</div>
                                    <InputFile OnChange="@OnInputFileChange"
                                               Accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp"
                                               Class="upload-input"
                                               Disabled="@(_isSubmitting || _isUploading)" />
                                </div>
                            }

                            @* Preview card — REPLACES the dropzone once the
                               user has picked a file. Shows a downscaled
                               thumbnail (generated client-side from the
                               IBrowserFile via RequestImageFileAsync), the
                               filename + size, and a Remove button. The
                               actual upload happens later, on submit. *@
                            @if (_selectedFile is not null)
                            {
                                <div class="preview-card">
                                    <div class="preview-img-wrap">
                                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_previewDataUrl))
                                        {
                                            <img src="@_previewDataUrl"
                                                 alt="@Loc["PicturePreviewAlt"]"
                                                 class="preview-img" />
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="image"
                                                        Style="font-size: 2rem; color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="preview-info">
                                        <div class="preview-label">
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="check_circle" Style="color: var(--rz-success);" />
                                            @Loc["PictureSelected"]
                                        </div>
                                        <span class="preview-url">@_selectedFile.Name · @FormatBytes(_selectedFile.Size)</span>
                                        <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);">
                                            @Loc["PictureSelectedHint"]
                                        </RadzenText>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="preview-actions">
                                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RemoveImage"]"
                                                      Icon="delete_outline"
                                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                                      Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                      Disabled="@(_isSubmitting || _isUploading)"
                                                      Click="@RemoveImage" />
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            }

                            <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); display: block; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
                                @Loc["PictureUrlHint"]
                            </RadzenText>

                            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_uploadError))
                            {
                                <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["UploadErrorTitle"]"
                                             Text="@_uploadError"
                                             ShowIcon="true"
                                             Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                             AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                             Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                            }
                        </div>

                        @* Form actions. Both buttons are disabled during
                           submit AND during the upload phase (which runs
                           as part of submit when a file is selected). The
                           submit button's icon swaps to a spinner during
                           upload so the user sees something is happening. *@
                        <div class="form-actions">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CancelButton"]"
                                          Icon="close"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                          Disabled="@(_isSubmitting || _isUploading)"
                                          Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
                            <RadzenButton Text="@(_isUploading ? Loc["UploadingButton"] : Loc["SubmitButton"])"
                                          Icon="@(_isUploading ? "hourglass_top" : "save")"
                                          ButtonType="ButtonType.Submit"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Disabled="@(_isSubmitting || _isUploading)" />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </EditForm>
            </RadzenCard>

            @* RIGHT — help panel (sticky on desktop) *@
            <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Class="help-panel" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.5rem" Style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                    <RadzenIcon Icon="help_outline" Style="color: var(--rz-primary);" />
                    <RadzenText Text="@Loc["HelpTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
                </RadzenStack>
                <ul>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpNameUnique"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpPrice"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpStock"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpCategory"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpPictureUrl"]</li>
                    <li>@Loc["HelpPurchaseLimits"]</li>
                </ul>
            </RadzenCard>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Form model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// View-model for the create-product form. NOT the same as the
    /// command — we keep the form flat (MoneyDto is split into Amount +
    /// Currency for simpler RadzenNumeric/RadzenDropDown binding) and
    /// assemble the MoneyDto + CreateProductCommand at submit time.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class CreateProductFormModel
    {
        // Validation attributes mirror CreateProductCommandValidator's rules
        // so the user gets immediate client-side feedback without a round-trip
        // to the server. The FluentValidation validator on the command still
        // runs server-side as defense-in-depth. Localized messages will be
        // wired in Phase 7 item D (FluentValidation LanguageManager); for
        // now, DataAnnotations' default English messages are shown by the
        // existing <ValidationMessage> components.

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Product name is required.")]
        [StringLength(200, ErrorMessage = "Product name cannot exceed 200 characters.")]
        public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Product description is required.")]
        [StringLength(2000, ErrorMessage = "Product description cannot exceed 2000 characters.")]
        public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;

        [Range(0.0001, double.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Product price must be greater than zero.")]
        public decimal PriceAmount { get; set; } = 1m;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Currency is required.")]
        [StringLength(3, MinimumLength = 3, ErrorMessage = "Currency must be a 3-letter ISO 4217 code (e.g. USD, IRR).")]
        public string PriceCurrency { get; set; } = "USD";

        [Range(0, 1_000_000, ErrorMessage = "Initial stock quantity must be between 0 and 1,000,000.")]
        public int InitialStockQuantity { get; set; } = 0;

        [Required(ErrorMessage = "Category ID is required.")]
        public Guid? CategoryId { get; set; }

        // No validation — SubCategoryId and SubSubCategoryId are optional.
        // The cross-field "cannot set SubSubCategory without SubCategory"
        // rule is enforced server-side by CreateProductCommandValidator.
        public Guid? SubCategoryId { get; set; }
        public Guid? SubSubCategoryId { get; set; }

        // PictureUrl is NOT on the form model. The picture is held in
        // memory as IBrowserFile? _selectedFile (captured by the
        // InputFile component) and only converted to a URL when the
        // user submits — the upload POSTs the file to /api/product-image
        // and the returned URL is passed directly to CreateProductCommand.
        // This avoids the orphan-files bug where picking an image without
        // submitting the form would leave a saved-but-unreferenced file
        // under wwwroot/uploads/products/.
    }

    private CreateProductFormModel _model = new();

    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private List<CategoryDto> _categories = new();
    private List<SubCategoryDto> _availableSubCategories = new();
    private List<SubSubCategoryDto> _availableSubSubCategories = new();

    private bool _isLoadingCategories = true;
    private string? _categoriesLoadError;
    private bool _isSubmitting;
    private string? _submitError;

    // ── Deferred image-upload state ─────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // The original implementation used RadzenUpload with Auto=true, which
    // immediately POSTed the selected file to /api/product-image and saved
    // it to disk. This produced orphan files whenever the user picked an
    // image but never submitted the form (cancelled, hit validation
    // errors, navigated away, etc.).
    //
    // The fix: capture the file in memory as an IBrowserFile (via
    // Blazor's InputFile component) and only POST it during the submit
    // handler. The file is held server-side in the Blazor circuit's
    // memory; nothing is written to disk until "Create product" is
    // clicked. If the user cancels or validation fails, no file is
    // saved.
    //
    // - _selectedFile:        the in-memory IBrowserFile picked by the
    //                          user. Null until they pick something,
    //                          cleared by RemoveImage or by picking a
    //                          new file (InputFile fires OnChange with
    //                          the new file, replacing the old).
    // - _previewDataUrl:      a downscaled data: URL generated client-
    //                          side via IBrowserFile.RequestImageFileAsync
    //                          (400×400 max). Used as the <img src> for
    //                          the preview thumbnail. Generation is best-
    //                          effort — if it fails (e.g. corrupt image),
    //                          we just show a generic icon instead.
    // - _alreadyUploadedUrl:  the URL returned by /api/product-image on a
    //                          previous successful upload attempt during
    //                          THIS form's lifetime. If the command then
    //                          fails (e.g. name not unique) and the user
    //                          retries, we reuse this URL instead of
    //                          re-uploading — avoiding duplicate orphan
    //                          files on retry. Cleared by RemoveImage and
    //                          by picking a new file (different file =
    //                          different upload needed).
    // - _uploadError:         validation/parse error message from the
    //                          file-selection step (bad type, too large,
    //                          etc.). Shown inline below the dropzone.
    // - _isUploading:         true during the POST to /api/product-image
    //                          inside HandleSubmitAsync. Disables both
    //                          buttons + the file input so the user can't
    //                          start a second upload mid-flight.
    private IBrowserFile? _selectedFile;
    private string? _previewDataUrl;
    private string? _alreadyUploadedUrl;
    private string? _uploadError;
    private bool _isUploading;

    /// <summary>
    /// Maximum accepted file size (matches LocalFileStorage's cap).
    /// Enforced client-side via IBrowserFile.Size check + OpenReadStream
    /// (which throws if the stream exceeds the limit).
    /// </summary>
    private const long MaxFileSize = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5 MB

    /// <summary>
    /// Content types accepted by the upload. Matches the allowlist in
    /// the /api/product-image endpoint (Program.cs) and in
    /// LocalFileStorage. Validated client-side here for immediate
    /// feedback; validated again server-side as defense-in-depth.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly HashSet<string> AllowedContentTypes = new(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
    {
        "image/jpeg", "image/png", "image/webp"
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// The most common ISO 4217 currency codes. The user can type a
    /// custom 3-letter code via the dropdown's AllowCustomValue=true.
    /// IRR (Iranian Rial) is included because the user's locale is fa-IR.
    /// </summary>
    private readonly List<string> _currencyOptions = new()
    {
      "IRR" , "EUR", "GBP", "USD", "JPY", "CNY", "AED", "TRY", "CAD", "AUD"
    };

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        await LoadCategoriesAsync();
    }

    // ── Image selection handlers ────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // InputFile (Blazor's built-in file picker) fires OnChange when the
    // user picks a file (or cancels the picker with no selection). We get
    // direct access to the IBrowserFile here — no upload happens yet.
    // The file is held in memory in the Blazor circuit; it's only POSTed
    // to /api/product-image inside HandleSubmitAsync when the user clicks
    // "Create product". This is the fix for the orphan-files bug.
    //
    // Validation here mirrors the server-side checks in /api/product-image
    // (Program.cs) and LocalFileStorage. Doing it client-side too gives
    // immediate feedback without a round-trip; the server-side checks
    // remain as defense-in-depth in case the client is bypassed.

    private async Task OnInputFileChange(InputFileChangeEventArgs e)
    {
        _uploadError = null;

        // User cancelled the OS file picker — keep the previous selection
        // (if any) intact. InputFile fires OnChange with FileCount==0 in
        // this case.
        if (e.FileCount == 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        var file = e.File;

        // ── Validate content type.
        if (!AllowedContentTypes.Contains(file.ContentType))
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["UploadInvalidType"];
            _selectedFile = null;
            _previewDataUrl = null;
            _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;
            return;
        }

        // ── Validate size.
        if (file.Size > MaxFileSize)
        {
            _uploadError = Loc["UploadInvalidSize"];
            _selectedFile = null;
            _previewDataUrl = null;
            _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;
            return;
        }

        // ── Accept the file. Clear any previous upload URL — picking a
        //    new file invalidates a previous successful upload (the old
        //    file is no longer the one we want associated with this
        //    product, so we can't reuse its /uploads/products/... path).
        _selectedFile = file;
        _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;
        _previewDataUrl = await GeneratePreviewDataUrlAsync(file);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Generates a downscaled data: URL preview of the selected image.
    /// Uses IBrowserFile.RequestImageFileAsync which produces a server-
    /// side resized copy (max 400×400) — keeps the data URL small
    /// (~50 KB even for multi-megabyte source images). Best-effort:
    /// returns null if preview generation fails (e.g. corrupt image);
    /// the UI then falls back to a generic icon.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task<string?> GeneratePreviewDataUrlAsync(IBrowserFile file)
    {
        try
        {
            // RequestImageFileAsync takes the target format, max width,
            // max height. It preserves aspect ratio within the bounds.
            // We pass the source content type so the resized image keeps
            // the same format (JPEG stays JPEG, etc.).
            var resized = await file.RequestImageFileAsync(file.ContentType, 400, 400);

            // OpenReadStream with a 2 MB cap is plenty for a 400×400
            // thumbnail. The cap is defense-in-depth against a malicious
            // file that lies about its dimensions to try to allocate a
            // huge buffer.
            await using var stream = resized.OpenReadStream(maxAllowedSize: 2 * 1024 * 1024);
            using var ms = new MemoryStream();
            await stream.CopyToAsync(ms);
            var base64 = Convert.ToBase64String(ms.ToArray());
            return $"data:{file.ContentType};base64,{base64}";
        }
        catch
        {
            // Non-fatal: preview is a UI nicety, not required for submit.
            // The actual file content is still uploaded to the server
            // (where LocalFileStorage does its own magic-byte sniffing
            // and will reject the file if it's genuinely corrupt).
            return null;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Clears the selected file + preview + any cached upload URL.
    /// Called by the "Remove" button on the preview card. After this,
    /// the user can pick a different image or just submit with no
    /// picture (PictureUrl is optional).
    /// </summary>
    private void RemoveImage()
    {
        _selectedFile = null;
        _previewDataUrl = null;
        _alreadyUploadedUrl = null;
        _uploadError = null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a byte count as a human-readable string (e.g. "1.2 MB").
    /// Used in the preview card to show the selected file's size.
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatBytes(long bytes)
    {
        string[] units = { "B", "KB", "MB", "GB" };
        double size = bytes;
        int unit = 0;
        while (size >= 1024 && unit < units.Length - 1)
        {
            size /= 1024;
            unit++;
        }
        return $"{size:0.#} {units[unit]}";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Uploads the selected file to /api/product-image. Returns the
    /// public URL on success, or an error message on failure. Called
    /// from HandleSubmitAsync — NOT from OnInputFileChange — so the
    /// file is only written to disk when the user actually submits the
    /// form.
    ///
    /// The endpoint returns:
    ///   200 OK       { "url": "/uploads/products/..." }
    ///   400/413/etc. { "error": "..." }
    /// </summary>
    private async Task<(string? Url, string? Error)> UploadSelectedFileAsync()
    {
        if (_selectedFile is null)
        {
            // Nothing to upload — caller should treat null URL as "no
            // picture on this product".
            return (Url: null, Error: null);
        }

        try
        {
            // OpenReadStream enforces the 5 MB cap server-side in the
            // Blazor circuit (separate from the IBrowserFile.Size check
            // we already did in OnInputFileChange). Passing the cap here
            // makes the stream throw IOExceededMemoryLimitException as
            // soon as the cumulative byte count crosses 5 MB, instead of
            // buffering the whole file first.
            await using var stream = _selectedFile.OpenReadStream(maxAllowedSize: MaxFileSize);

            using var content = new MultipartFormDataContent
            {
                { new StreamContent(stream), "file", _selectedFile.Name }
            };

            var response = await Http.PostAsync("/api/product-image", content);
            var responseJson = await response.Content.ReadAsStringAsync();

            if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode)
            {
                // Try to extract a server-provided error message from
                // { "error": "..." }. Fall back to a generic message.
                string? serverError = null;
                try
                {
                    using var doc = System.Text.Json.JsonDocument.Parse(responseJson);
                    if (doc.RootElement.TryGetProperty("error", out var errProp))
                    {
                        serverError = errProp.GetString();
                    }
                }
                catch
                {
                    // Response wasn't JSON — leave serverError null and
                    // fall through to the generic message.
                }

                return (Url: null, Error: serverError ?? Loc["UploadErrorGeneric"]);
            }

            // Parse { "url": "/uploads/products/..." } from the 200 body.
            string? url = null;
            try
            {
                using var doc = System.Text.Json.JsonDocument.Parse(responseJson);
                if (doc.RootElement.TryGetProperty("url", out var urlProp))
                {
                    url = urlProp.GetString();
                }
            }
            catch
            {
                // JSON parse failure on a 200 response is a server bug.
                // Treat as a malformed-response error.
            }

            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(url))
            {
                return (Url: null, Error: Loc["UploadErrorResponseFormat"]);
            }

            return (Url: url, Error: null);
        }
        catch
        {
            // Network failure, request cancellation, stream size limit,
            // etc. Don't leak exception details — return a generic message.
            return (Url: null, Error: Loc["UploadErrorGeneric"]);
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadCategoriesAsync()
    {
        _isLoadingCategories = true;
        _categoriesLoadError = null;

        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<List<CategoryDto>>>(
                new GetActiveCategoriesQuery());

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _categories = result.Value;
            }
            else
            {
                _categoriesLoadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            _categoriesLoadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoadingCategories = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Cascade handlers ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// When the user picks a Category (or clears it), recompute the
    /// available SubCategories and clear any selected Sub/SubSub.
    /// </summary>
    private Task OnCategoryChanged(Guid? categoryId)
    {
        _model.CategoryId = categoryId;
        _model.SubCategoryId = null;
        _model.SubSubCategoryId = null;

        _availableSubCategories = categoryId is null
            ? new()
            : _categories.FirstOrDefault(c => c.Id == categoryId.Value)?.SubCategories ?? new();

        _availableSubSubCategories = new();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// When the user picks a SubCategory (or clears it), recompute the
    /// available SubSubCategories and clear any selected SubSub.
    /// </summary>
    private Task OnSubCategoryChanged(Guid? subCategoryId)
    {
        _model.SubCategoryId = subCategoryId;
        _model.SubSubCategoryId = null;

        _availableSubSubCategories = subCategoryId is null
            ? new()
            : _availableSubCategories.FirstOrDefault(sc => sc.Id == subCategoryId.Value)?.SubSubCategories ?? new();

        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    // ── Submit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Submit is now a TWO-PHASE operation when a file is selected:
    //   Phase 1 (upload): POST the selected file to /api/product-image,
    //                      get back the public URL it's been saved at.
    //                      Sets _isUploading=true to disable all buttons.
    //   Phase 2 (create): Dispatch CreateProductCommand with the uploaded
    //                      URL (or null if no file was selected). Standard
    //                      Wolverine pipeline.
    //
    // If Phase 1 fails, we abort before Phase 2 — no product is created
    // and the file error is shown above the form. If Phase 1 succeeds
    // but Phase 2 fails (e.g. name not unique), we cache the uploaded
    // URL in _alreadyUploadedUrl so a retry skips Phase 1 — otherwise
    // each retry would upload a fresh copy and leave orphan files.

    private async Task HandleSubmitAsync()
    {
        // Clear previous server-side error. The EditForm has already
        // validated the model (DataAnnotationsValidator), so we only
        // reach this handler if client-side validation passed.
        _submitError = null;

        // Defense: re-check the required CategoryId. The dropdown binding
        // is to Guid?, so a null is possible if the user didn't pick one.
        if (_model.CategoryId is null || _model.CategoryId == Guid.Empty)
        {
            _submitError = Loc["Error_CategoryRequired"];
            return;
        }

        _isSubmitting = true;

        try
        {
            // ── Phase 1: upload the selected file (if any) ──
            // Reuse _alreadyUploadedUrl if it's set — this happens when
            // a previous submit attempt uploaded the file successfully
            // but the create command failed. Re-uploading would create
            // a second orphan file under /uploads/products/.
            string? pictureUrl = _alreadyUploadedUrl;
            if (pictureUrl is null && _selectedFile is not null)
            {
                _isUploading = true;
                try
                {
                    var (url, error) = await UploadSelectedFileAsync();
                    if (error is not null)
                    {
                        // Upload failed — abort the whole submit. The user
                        // can fix the issue (pick a smaller file, etc.) and
                        // retry. The selected file is still in memory so
                        // they don't need to re-pick.
                        _submitError = error;
                        return;
                    }
                    pictureUrl = url;
                    _alreadyUploadedUrl = url; // cache for retry
                }
                finally
                {
                    _isUploading = false;
                }
            }

            // ── Phase 2: dispatch the create command ──
            var command = new CreateProductCommand(
                Name: _model.Name.Trim(),
                Description: _model.Description.Trim(),
                PictureUrl: pictureUrl,
                Price: new MoneyDto
                {
                    Amount = _model.PriceAmount,
                    Currency = _model.PriceCurrency.Trim().ToUpperInvariant()
                },
                InitialStockQuantity: _model.InitialStockQuantity,
                CategoryId: _model.CategoryId.Value,
                SubCategoryId: _model.SubCategoryId,
                SubSubCategoryId: _model.SubSubCategoryId);

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<Guid>>(command);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["CreateSuccess"], _model.Name),
                    summary: Loc["CreateSuccessTitle"]);

                // Navigate back to the admin list — the new product will
                // appear at the top (sorted by name asc, so position
                // depends on alphabetical order).
                Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products", forceLoad: false);
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains a user-friendly message from the
                // handler (e.g. "A product with the name 'X' already exists.
                // Choose a different name." OR "Category '...' was not found."
                // OR "SubCategory '...' does not belong to Category '...'.")
                //
                // NOTE: if Phase 1 uploaded a file, that file is now an
                // orphan on disk (no product references it). We accept this
                // trade-off — the alternative (rolling back the upload by
                // deleting the file) would require tracking the file's
                // identity, which LocalFileStorage doesn't expose. The
                // orphan rate is now ~0% on the happy path (upload only
                // happens at submit time) and only happens on the rare
                // command-fails-after-successful-upload path. A future
                // cleanup task can sweep /uploads/products/ for files not
                // referenced by any Product.PictureUrl.
                _submitError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericCreate"];
            }
        }
        catch (FluentValidation.ValidationException vex)
        {
            // Validation failures from CreateProductCommandValidator (and
            // any other validator Wolverine runs before the handler). Each
            // failure.ErrorMessage is already localized by
            // TakOneLanguageManager (Phase 7 item D) via the "@"-prefixed
            // resource key in .WithMessage(...). Join them with newline
            // so the UI can render multi-line errors.
            _submitError = vex.GetJoinedMessages();
        }
        catch
        {
            // Any other exception (network, DI, handler-thrown) — surface a
            // generic localized message. The actual exception is logged by
            // Wolverine's LoggingMiddleware.
            _submitError = Loc["Error_GenericCreate"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isSubmitting = false;
        }
    }
}